// Secrets.xcconfig.example — template for the iOS app's build-time secrets.
//
// The real file (Secrets.xcconfig) is gitignored and must NEVER be committed.
//
// SETUP (one-time, before a release build):
//   1. Copy this file:            cp Secrets.xcconfig.example Secrets.xcconfig
//   2. Fill in API_KEY below with the SAME value you set as APP_API_KEY on the
//      backend (Render env var). It must match, or every request will 401.
//   3. In Xcode: select the project → "smartmarket" target → Info tab →
//      "Configurations" → set this Secrets.xcconfig as the Debug and Release
//      base configuration file (or set it on the project so all targets inherit).
//   4. In smartmarket/Info.plist change the API_KEY value to:  $(API_KEY)
//      so the build substitutes this value into the shipped Info.plist.
//
// Leaving API_KEY empty disables auth (dev only). See SECURITY.md for the
// longer-term plan (per-device tokens + App Attest) that replaces this shared key.

API_KEY =
